# WardenClyffe Parking-Lot Rule (forced)

Whenever the conversation turns to planning, scoping, roadmaps, sprints, POAMs,
trade-offs, or **locking in** any dependency, feature, capability, library,
service, protocol, schema, or boundary — enter Parking-Lot mode, even if the
operator never typed `/parkinglot`.

Follow `docs/ai/WARDENCLYFFE_PARKING_LOT_SKILL.md`.

When a decision is locked in, capture it via
`scripts/foundation/parking-lot-capture.py` (it writes a v2 `clyffy_touchpoint`
that the sync worker projects into Qdrant + SurrealDB). Never write to a
database by hand.

Before creating any new folder/boundary, defer to the boundary-guard rule and
`docs/ai/WARDENCLYFFE_BOUNDARY_GUARD_SKILL.md`.
